        "title": "feat(provider): add Sealos Devbox SSH-lease provider",
        "body": "Closes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/365\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds `sealos-devbox` as a Crabbox Linux SSH-lease provider backed by Sealos DevBox lifecycle resources.\n\nThis includes provider registration and configuration, read-only doctor checks, CRD create/resolve/status/release/cleanup paths, exact scope- and claim-bound ownership checks, controller-owned Secret validation, SSH routing, guarded live-smoke wiring, documentation, and regression coverage.\n\n## Lifecycle safety\n\n- Uses conflict-safe `kubectl create` and reconciles ambiguous results only when the live DevBox exactly matches the requested scope, lease, and slug.\n- Revalidates scope, lease, slug, UID, and Kubernetes `resourceVersion` before destructive operations.\n- Fails closed on inventory and identity errors; stale local claims are discarded only after direct absence proof.\n- Reads key material only from the exact controller-owned DevBox Secret and persists it only in Crabbox's local lease key store.\n- Keeps status and doctor read-only; tenant-safe API discovery and one `SelfSubjectRulesReview` check permissions without provider mutation.\n- The guarded live smoke now uses delete-on-release and requires empty exact lease/slug inventory after stop, preventing a successful test from leaving a billable paused DevBox.\n- Preserves the full ownership fingerprint in annotations across touch operations; Kubernetes-safe labels remain truncated independently.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Exact candidate: `c61a02c1eb369517a349ef302796a128326090d1`\n- Rebased onto `main` at `5b39acb1d8d0530824f1acc25d73b94bc9a0c773`.\n- `go test -race -timeout 20m ./...`\n- `go vet ./...`\n- `go build -trimpath -o /tmp/crabbox-sealos-final ./cmd/crabbox`\n- `node --test scripts/live-smoke.test.js` (54 passing)\n- Worker format, lint, typecheck, tests (866 passing, 3 skipped), and dry-run build\n- docs site build\n- `git diff --check`\n- local AutoReview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings (0.87 confidence)\n- Current upstream contract cross-check: [DevBox v1alpha2 types](https://github.com/labring/sealos/blob/main/controllers/devbox/api/v1alpha2/devbox_types.go), [controller Secret generation](https://github.com/labring/sealos/blob/main/controllers/devbox/internal/controller/devbox_sync_pipeline.go), and [SSHGate public-key forwarding](https://github.com/labring/sealos/blob/main/service/sshgate/gateway/publickey.go).\n\n## Authenticated live proof\n\n- Provider: hosted Sealos DevBox, US West tenant, SSHGate port 2233.\n- Exact candidate: `c61a02c1eb369517a349ef302796a128326090d1`.\n- Disposable lease: `cbx_fbd485f4fc75`; DevBox: `crabbox-sealos-pr682-live5-46cbb42b`.\n- Passed tenant-scoped doctor/API discovery/RBAC, create, SSH readiness, missing-tool bootstrap, status, SSH command generation, 1,382-file sync, real remote command, ownership touch, guarded delete, and final cleanup dry-run.\n- Remote command returned `crabbox-live-ok` from the synced repository workdir.\n- Zero residue verified through the Kubernetes API, local claim/key state, and the rendered Sealos DevBox dashboard empty state.\n\nEarlier disposable canaries exposed and verified the hosted scheduling contract, SSHGate port, base-image tool requirements, missing-resource cleanup, and a 64-to-63-character ownership annotation truncation. Each was cleaned; the final fresh lifecycle passed after the fixes.\n",
